  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: cxf-rt-transports-jms 3.6.9.rhlw-00004",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.cxf:cxf-rt-transports-jms 3.6.9.rhlw-00004 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-44417, CVE-2026-50632, and CVE-2026-66909.\n\nCVE-2026-44417: Apache CXF: Incomplete fix for CVE-2025-48913 (Untrusted JMS configuration can lead to RCE)\n\nCVE-2026-50632: Apache CXF: JNDI Injection Vulnerability in JMSConfigFactory\n\nCVE-2026-66909: Apache CXF: Unsafe deserialization of inbound JMS ObjectMessage\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.cxf:cxf-rt-transports-jms 3.6.9 from Maven Central.",
